labfigs includes or adapts material from the projects below. Their licence texts follow.

1. Andrey Churkin, BeautifulFigures (https://github.com/AndreyChurkin/BeautifulFigures), MIT:
   the design checklist, fine grid, purple-teal set, sunset ramp, dark page and example layouts.
2. Matt DesLauriers, dictionary-of-colour-combinations
   (https://github.com/mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations), MIT:
   the 348 numbered combinations in labfigs_combos.py, after Sanzo Wada.
3. ColorSchemes.jl (https://github.com/JuliaGraphics/ColorSchemes.jl), MIT:
   the named schemes in labfigs_combos.py. Its licence file below also covers the schemes it
   carries from matplotlib, ColorBrewer (Apache 2.0, colours by Cynthia Brewer,
   https://colorbrewer2.org; BrBG and PRGn among them) and cmocean (MIT; dense and tempo
   among them). Schemes longer than the lists here were sampled at evenly spaced stops.
4. Fabio Crameri, Scientific colour maps (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1243862), MIT:
   bilbao, devon, lajolla, oslo, turku, acton, tokyo, lipari, navia, davos, grayC, vik, broc,
   cork, berlin, tofino, vikO, brocO and corkO, via ColorSchemes.jl. Papers that use them
   should cite Crameri, F. (2018), Scientific colour maps, Zenodo.
5. Paul Tol, colour schemes (https://sronpersonalpages.nl/~pault/), BSD 3-Clause:
   tol_bright and tol_muted, via ColorSchemes.jl.

The house style follows the figures of Kairui Hao's thesis; no material from it is included.

